Z||000001||JohnnyK||11-30-2000||05:11 PM||||It's probably not tight. Get to the back and tighten the adjustor (almost smack in the middle of the back). It's probably not gonna budge without some heat though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||11-30-2000||05:12 PM||||Put your car up on stands...take off the 2 back tires and then follow the ebrake cable back to the tires...get a friend to pull the e-brake well u watch what happens...most likely something is wrong at the disc e-brake assembly...if so then replace them or ajust them so that it pulls and presses the pads on the rotors...<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
